          "text": "{\"stories\":[{\"id\":\"s000014\",\"rating\":{\"coherence\":7,\"style\":5,\"grammar\":8,\"storytelling\":6,\"overall\":6},\"note\":\"The search, teacher’s retrieval, and shared drawing make sense, though “saved the moon atlas” is unclear and the ending is slight.\",\"group_id\":0},{\"id\":\"s000028\",\"rating\":{\"coherence\":8,\"style\":6,\"grammar\":9,\"storytelling\":7,\"overall\":7},\"note\":\"Mina gives up her own sketch to help find Jun’s book, then they turn it into a shared drawing; the choice and payoff are clear.\",\"group_id\":1},{\"id\":\"s000058\",\"rating\":{\"coherence\":8,\"style\":6,\"grammar\":9,\"storytelling\":7,\"overall\":7},\"note\":\"Mina puts aside her moon sketch to help Jun, and the recovered whale book leads to a concrete drawing together.\",\"group_id\":1},{\"id\":\"s000023\",\"rating\":{\"coherence\":7,\"style\":5,\"grammar\":8,\"storytelling\":6,\"overall\":6},\"note\":\"The events resolve the missing-book problem and end with a moon drawing, but “saved the moon atlas” is awkwardly vague.\",\"group_id\":0},{\"id\":\"s000036\",\"rating\":{\"coherence\":8,\"style\":6,\"grammar\":9,\"storytelling\":7,\"overall\":7},\"note\":\"A clear helping choice leads to Jun’s book being retrieved and Mina making a whale drawing, though the prose is event-like.\",\"group_id\":1},{\"id\":\"s000017\",\"rating\":{\"coherence\":7,\"style\":5,\"grammar\":9,\"storytelling\":6,\"overall\":6},\"note\":\"The teacher retrieves the whale book while Mina’s atlas is preserved, allowing the original moon-sketch goal to conclude; the choice is not explained.\",\"group_id\":0},{\"id\":\"s000053\",\"rating\":{\"coherence\":8,\"style\":6,\"grammar\":9,\"storytelling\":7,\"overall\":7},\"note\":\"Mina chooses to help Jun, and the recovered book becomes the basis for a whale drawing; the ending is concrete but brisk.\",\"group_id\":1},{\"id\":\"s000021\",\"rating\":{\"coherence\":7,\"style\":5,\"grammar\":9,\"storytelling\":6,\"overall\":6},\"note\":\"The book is retrieved and Mina completes her moon sketch, but “saved the moon atlas” leaves the teacher’s action unclear.\",\"group_id\":0},{\"id\":\"s000034\",\"rating\":{\"coherence\":7,\"style\":5,\"grammar\":9,\"storytelling\":6,\"overall\":6},\"note\":\"Jun’s book is found and Mina finishes her moon drawing, though the atlas being “saved” is not clearly motivated.\",\"group_id\":0},{\"id\":\"s000048\",\"rating\":{\"coherence\":8,\"style\":6,\"grammar\":9,\"storytelling\":7,\"overall\":7},\"note\":\"Mina prioritizes helping Jun, then uses his recovered whale book for a drawing that closes the exchange.\",\"group_id\":1}],\"diversity\":{\"premise\":2,\"causal_path\":2,\"ending\":2,\"language\":2,\"overall\":2},\"diversity_evidence\":\"All ten share the same library premise, search for Jun’s missing whale book, high-shelf retrieval by Ms Alvarez, and drawing finale. The small causal split is whether Mina’s own moon-atlas goal is preserved while help is provided (s000014, s000023, s000017, s000021, s000034) or she sets it aside and draws a whale from Jun’s book (s000028, s000058, s000036, s000053, s000048). These are minor branch variations, not distinct plot families; the set alone does not establish diversity of the generator.\",\"plot_groups\":[{\"group_id\":0,\"summary\":\"Mina wants to sketch the moon but promises to help Jun find his missing whale book; the teacher retrieves it while Mina’s moon atlas is preserved, and Mina completes a moon drawing.\"},{\"group_id\":1,\"summary\":\"Mina sets aside her moon sketch to help Jun find his missing whale book; after the teacher retrieves it, Mina draws a whale from Jun’s book.\"}]}",
